# Local gate. Two halves, cheapest first:
#
#   1. mechanical, per-file    prettier on staged files
#   2. mechanical, whole-repo  tsc + eslint, then fallow's changed-code verdict
#
# There is no CI in this repo (no .github/workflows/), so nothing runs any of
# this a second time on push. If a check is not here, it is not running.

bunx lint-staged
bun run typecheck
bun run lint

# fallow: dead exports, complexity, duplication, styling on changed code.
#
# `--base HEAD` deliberately replaces fallow's shipped `merge-base @{upstream}`
# base. That base asks "does this BRANCH introduce a finding?", which at commit
# time re-reports every finding from every earlier commit on the branch and
# blocks work unrelated to the edit in hand. `HEAD` asks the pre-commit
# question: "does THIS commit introduce one?" The branch-wide question belongs
# to a pre-push or CI tier, which this repo does not have yet.
#
# Silent on pass, full report on fail. Skipped when fallow is not installed, so
# the hook stays portable.
command -v fallow >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0
fallow audit --base HEAD --quiet --gate-marker pre-commit
